/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Think of a slab on four edges as two sets of crossing strips that must deflect the same amount where they cross.
   - IS 456 therefore designs a slab with ly/lx > 2 as one-way: only the short-span strips are designed for bending, and the long direction gets the minimum steel.
   - A load of w kN/m² on the slab is a line load of w kN/m on a 1 m strip, the same number.
   - wu is the factored load, 1.5 × (dead + live), in kN/m on the strip; l is the effective span in m.
   - This is the Annex G equation Mu = 0.87 fy Ast d (1 − Ast fy/(b d fck)) solved for Ast, valid while Mu ≤ Mu,lim = 0.138 fck b d² (Fe415).
   - Distribution steel runs along the long span, on top of the main bars, which stay in the outer layer to keep the larger d.
*/
