/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Let lx be the short effective span and ly the long one.
   - A continuous edge is one where the slab carries on over the beam into the next panel; it has a hogging (negative) moment and needs top steel.
   - Both use lx², the short span. αx varies with ly/lx (interpolate between columns); αy is one value for each case, in the last column of Table 26.
*/
