/* book Worked example 2: Q: A roof slab 3.5 m × 4.2 m (effective) rests on walls on all four sides; its corners are not held down. wu = 10.5 kN/m², dx = 96 mm, dy = 88 mm. Find Mx, My and the steel.
   1. r = 4.2/3.5 = 1.20. Table 27: αx = 0.084, αy = 0.059.
   2. Mx = 0.084 × 10.5 × 3.5² = 10.80 kN·m/m; My = 0.059 × 10.5 × 3.5² = 7.59 kN·m/m.
   3. Ast: short span 336 mm²/m (8 mm @ 140), long span 254 mm²/m (8 mm @ 190). No torsion steel.
   Answer: Mx = 10.80 and My = 7.59 kN·m/m. The same panel with corners held down and two adjacent edges continuous would have a mid-span Mx of only 5.79 kN·m/m. */
